From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@localhost>
Date: Sat Oct 31 12:30:00 2026 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pci: sky1-cix: release init mutex on power-enable timeout

The x2/x1 branch of sky1_pcie_set_pwr_en() takes sky1_init_mutex
before polling the power-enable status bit, but returns -ETIMEDOUT on
timeout without unlocking it.  All later clock, reset, PHY and
enumeration helpers take the same mutex, so a single power-enable
timeout deadlocks the remaining PCIe controller probes and suspend/
resume paths instead of failing that one controller.

Unlock before returning.

Signed-off-by: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@localhost>
---
 0180-pci-sky1-cix-unlock-on-pwren-timeout.patch | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c
@@ -915,6 +915,7 @@
 				ret = readl_poll_timeout(status_addr, read, !!(read&0x200), 5, 100);
 				if (ret) {
 					dev_err(dev, "Set pwr en err, 0x%x\n", read);
+					mutex_unlock(&sky1_init_mutex);
 					return -ETIMEDOUT;
 				}
 
